# Magpie Cloud

LLM orchestration backend for the Magpie desktop app. Holds the system
prompts and proxies LLM calls so the desktop app never ships them.

## What lives here

```
server/
├── magpie_server/
│   ├── main.py            FastAPI app + /health + /whoami
│   ├── auth.py            Invite-code bearer-token middleware
│   ├── settings.py        Env-var-driven config (pydantic-settings)
│   ├── prompts.py         (Phase 2.5 step 3) system prompts — the IP
│   └── llm_routes.py      (Phase 2.5 step 4) /llm/rewrite, /llm/answer, /llm/summarize
├── tests/
├── pyproject.toml         Server-only deps (no torch / qdrant / colpali)
├── .env.example           Copy to .env, fill in INVITE_CODES + OPENROUTER_API_KEY
├── Dockerfile             (Phase 2.5 step 7) for fly.io / Render / Railway
└── README.md              You are here.
```

## Run locally (dev)

```bash
# One-time: install server-only deps in a separate venv
cd server
uv sync                       # installs from server/pyproject.toml

# Configure
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env: set INVITE_CODES (or leave empty for unauth localhost)
#            set OPENROUTER_API_KEY (later — empty for skeleton testing)

# Run
uv run uvicorn magpie_server.main:app --reload
# → server now on http://127.0.0.1:8000
```

Or from the repo root:

```bash
just cloud-serve
```

## Smoke test

```bash
# Health (no auth needed)
curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/health

# Auth path (needs an invite code in INVITE_CODES env)
curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/whoami \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer your-invite-code"
```

## Auth model (beta)

Single shared-secret per beta tester. Generate codes with:

```bash
python -c "import secrets; print('alice-' + secrets.token_urlsafe(16))"
```

Add to `INVITE_CODES` (comma-separated). Hand the code to the tester; their
desktop app pastes it once at first launch.

To revoke a tester: drop their code from the env var, restart the server.

When Beta graduates to public launch, swap `auth.py` for JWT/OAuth — the
endpoint signatures don't change, only the dependency.

## Deploy

(Phase 2.5 step 7 — not built yet.) Will use fly.io's free tier:

```bash
fly launch                          # one-time
fly secrets set INVITE_CODES=...    # set per-tester codes
fly secrets set OPENROUTER_API_KEY=...
fly deploy                          # ship it
```

## Why this is in the same repo as the desktop app

See [../IO/IO - Repo Structure.md](../IO/IO%20-%20Repo%20Structure.md). Short
version: solo-dev coordination wins; we'll split this out only when we
hit one of the four legitimate triggers (people / product / license /
compliance).
